  <section class="split" aria-labelledby="r-how">
    <div class="prose">
      <h2 id="r-how">How I work</h2>
      <p>Most of my experiments run in gas-phase packed-bed microreactors that I set up and operate: liquid oxygenates are fed by syringe pump into hydrogen, vaporized in a heated pre-heater, passed over a small bed of catalyst, and analyzed online by gas chromatography.</p>
      <p>Before trusting a rate, I check for internal and external mass-transfer limits so the numbers reflect surface chemistry. I then pair the kinetics with characterization of fresh and spent catalysts to connect what the rates show to what has changed on the catalyst.</p>
      <ul class="chips">
        <li>Packed-bed kinetics</li><li>Rate laws and mechanism</li><li>Online GC / GC-MS</li><li>TPR · TPD · pulse titration</li><li>BET</li><li>XRD</li><li>XPS</li><li>Raman · FTIR</li><li>SEM · TEM</li><li>Python · JMP · DoE</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
